### 4.9 Systematic uncertainties

So far in this chapter, all of the results were described with only statistical uncertainties. Here, we describe other sources of uncertainties that may arise from the used method of analysis, the detector, etc. We will discuss the uncertainties one by one:

#### Tracking and PID uncertainties

The uncertainty of the TPC tracking was evaluated from embedding studies [90]. It was estimated as 3 % for a single track. The TOF-matching uncertainty comes from a variation of the matching efficiency with pileup, as discussed in Section 4.7.2. This uncertainty is evaluated as 3 % at the single-track level. The evaluation of the PID efficiency uncertainty is described in Section 4.7.3 and comes from from the difference between bin counting and fit of the Gaussian \({\rm d}E/{\rm d}x\) and TOF distributions. It is evaluated as 2 % per track.

#### Uncertainty of the yield extraction

